A lazy screen publishes its placeholder before its first frame, and the
placeholder carries no root sentinel. The bridge read the screen's first frame
after it as a stack mounting cold, reset the navigation coordinator, and made
the pushed screen the root: it drew the hand-drawn back chevron, and going back
pushed the screen beneath on top of it instead of returning to it. The stack is
taken to mount cold only where the last frame that had a sentinel was not a
stack's, so the plain frames a screen draws while it opens leave its place in
the stack as it was.

--- a/vendor/nativephp/mobile/resources/xcode/NativePHP/NativeRender/NativeElementBridge.swift
+++ b/vendor/nativephp/mobile/resources/xcode/NativePHP/NativeRender/NativeElementBridge.swift
@@ -125 +125,5 @@
     private static var nativeChromePrevTrees: [String: NativeUITree] = [:]
+
+    /// The root sentinel of the last tree that carried one, kept across the
+    /// plain frames a lazy screen publishes while it opens.
+    private static var lastChromeRootType: String?
@@ -420,2 +424,5 @@
             let isFreshStackMount =
-                newRootType == "native_root_stack" && prevRootType != "native_root_stack"
+                newRootType == "native_root_stack" && lastChromeRootType != "native_root_stack"
+            if newRootType == "native_root_stack" || newRootType == "native_root_tabs" {
+                lastChromeRootType = newRootType
+            }
